31:["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":["$","code",null,{"children":"worker_api_endpoint"}]}]," is the address of the ",["$","em",null,{"children":"scheduler's"}]," ",["$","code",null,{"children":"worker_api"}],"\nservice, the private port from\n",["$","$L1b",null,{"href":"/configuration/servers-and-services","children":"Servers and services"}],", not the public\none. The worker dials out; the scheduler never dials in. That direction is why\na worker fleet can sit behind NAT with no inbound rules."]}]
32:["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":["$","code",null,{"children":"cas_fast_slow_store"}]}]," must name a ",["$","code",null,{"children":"fast_slow"}]," store whose ",["$","code",null,{"children":"fast"}]," half is a\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"filesystem"}]," store. The worker builds each action's input tree by hard-linking\nfiles out of that fast store into the work directory, which requires real\nfiles on a real filesystem. The ",["$","code",null,{"children":"slow"}]," half must eventually resolve to the\nsame CAS the client and scheduler use, or be a ",["$","code",null,{"children":"noop"}],", when the fast tier is\nthe only storage."]}]
