57:["$","$L64",null,{"children":[["$","$L65",null,{"title":"Can one process be both scheduler and worker?","id":"can-one-process-be-both-scheduler-and-worker","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["Yes, and that's what ",["$","code",null,{"children":"forge-config/examples/basic_cas.json5"}]," is: one\nprocess with stores, a scheduler, a worker, a public server on ",["$","code",null,{"children":":50051"}]," and a\nprivate one on ",["$","code",null,{"children":":50061"}],". It's the right shape for a laptop and for testing.\nSplitting into separate processes is a deployment change, not a config\nrewrite; the same blocks move into separate files."]}]}],["$","$L65",null,{"title":"How do I run more than one worker?","id":"how-do-i-run-more-than-one-worker","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["Run more worker processes. The ",["$","code",null,{"children":"workers"}]," array can hold several entries in one\nprocess, but they share the machine, so the useful form of scaling is more\nmachines each running a worker config that dials the same scheduler. Nothing\non the scheduler side changes."]}]}],["$","$L65",null,{"title":"What does `entrypoint` do?","id":"what-does-entrypoint-do","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["It wraps every action. The configured command is prepended to the action's own\ncommand, so an ",["$","code",null,{"children":"entrypoint"}]," of ",["$","code",null,{"children":"run.sh"}]," and an action of ",["$","code",null,{"children":"sleep 5"}]," executes\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"run.sh sleep 5"}],". It's how you put actions inside a sandbox, a container, or a\ntimeout wrapper without the client knowing."]}]}],["$","$L65",null,{"title":"Why did my action fail with a timeout the client didn't ask for?","id":"why-did-my-action-fail-with-a-timeout-the-client-didnt-ask-for","children":[["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","code",null,{"children":"max_action_timeout_s"}]," on the worker defaults to 20 minutes. An action that\nrequests no timeout gets that limit; an action that requests a ",["$","em",null,{"children":"longer"}]," one is\nrejected outright with ",["$","code",null,{"children":"InvalidArgument: Action timeout of N seconds is greater than the maximum allowed timeout"}],". Either way, an action legitimately\nneeding longer needs this raised on the worker, not just on the client."]}],["$","a",null,{"href":"https://github.com/toxicwind/forge/blob/v1.6.5/forge-worker/src/running_actions_manager.rs","target":"_blank","rel":"noreferrer","data-source-link":"forge-worker/src/running_actions_manager.rs","data-source-ref":"v1.6.5","title":"forge-worker/src/running_actions_manager.rs at v1.6.5","className":"inline-flex items-center gap-1 rounded-md border border-border bg-surface-elevated px-1.5 py-0.5 align-middle font-mono text-xs text-muted-foreground no-underline transition-colors hover:border-brand/50 hover:text-brand","children":[["$","svg",null,{"width":"12","height":"12","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","aria-hidden":"true","children":["$","path",null,{"d":"m16 18 6-6-6-6M8 6l-6 6 6 6"}]}],"max_action_timeout"]}]]}],["$","$L65",null,{"title":"What is `experimental_precondition_script` for?","id":"what-is-experimental_precondition_script-for","children":["$","p",null,{"children":"It runs before every action, and a non-zero exit pauses the worker; it stops\naccepting new work until the script succeeds. The intended use is resource\ngating: don't take another action while disk is nearly full or a shared\nresource is saturated."}]}]]}]
